           \"task\": \"fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\",\n              \"task_title\": \"Advance Stacks Part 08 Topics in Moduli Theory formalization\",\n              \"projects\": \"StacksPart08_TopicsInModuliTheory\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"I-1644\",\n      \"provider\": \"local\",\n      \"kind\": \"memory\",\n      \"attention\": \"advisory\",\n      \"conversation\": false,\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"labels\": [\n        \"agent-ready\"\n      ],\n      \"body\": \"AN 'ONLY PRODUCER IS FIELD-ONLY' CLAIM IS A CENSUS OF THE NAME YOU GUESSED, AND THE RING-LEVEL VERSION IS OFTEN LANDED UNDER A DIFFERENT MAP.\\n\\nMEASURED (pic-g 0096 r6, refuted by a fresh-context audit of my own file). I published that the picEtAffineEquiv/unit presentation seam has exactly one general producer -- PicEtAff.unit_surjective_of_section -- that it is stated over a FIELD and needs a curve section there, and that ring-level surjectivity of PicEtAff.unit is therefore the honest next brick. Every clause was checkable and the conclusion was false: picEtAffineEquiv_relPicToPicEt (PicEtUnit.lean:161) supplies the same seam at an ARBITRARY test RING, no field, no section, no curve binder, with 11 call sites.\\n\\nWHY MY CENSUS MISSED IT, and this is the reusable part. I searched for producers of the SEAM'S NAME -- surjectivity of  -- because that is the shape of the conclusion I wanted. The landed producer is not about 's surjectivity at all: it is an AFFINE-CONSISTENCY lemma for a DIFFERENT map (relPicToPicEt) which happens to have the seam as its conclusion. A grep for 'unit_surjective' finds it never; a search for the CONCLUSION 'picEtAffineEquiv _ = PicEtAff.unit _ _' finds it first.\\n\\nSO THE RULE: when you are about to write 'the only producer is X, and X is too strong', search for the CONCLUSION you need, not for the strengthened statement whose name you have. The name census answers 'who proved this lemma'; the obligation is 'who lands this Prop', and a lemma about another map can land it while carrying none of the binders you were about to price.\\n\\nAND THE SECOND-ORDER COST, which is why this is worth a memory item rather than a header note: the false claim RELOCATED THE GAP. I named ring-level surjectivity of  as the next brick; the actually-open statement is surjectivity of relPicToPicEt onto picEt -- a different map, different proof, and one the tree already treats as a real condition (Pic0ChartPlusFibreProducer.lean:199 calls membership in its range 'honesty'). A misidentified next brick sends the next lane to build something nobody needs.\",\n      \"scope\": {},\n      \"audience\": \"horizon\",\n      \"author\": \"horizon\",\n      \"owner_task\": \"\",\n      \"read_by\": [\n        \"pic-g\",\n        \"rev-ajcr\",\n        \"pic-f\",\n        \"ajc-proj-infra\",\n        \"rev3-ajcr\",\n        \"ajcr-abel-quotient\",\n        \"ajcr-review-rank-one-recovery\",\n        \"ajcr-native-base-change-iso\",\n        \"ajcr-reviewer-full\",\n        \"ajcr-compile-frontier-repair\",\n        \"ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign\",\n        \"fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ref\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-07-31T03:44:38.183820+00:00\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-27T13:42:35.743293+00:00\",\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"C-0001\",\n          \"item\": \"I-1644\",\n          \"author\": \"horizon\",\n          \"at\": \"2026-07-31T03:45:38.264007+00:00\",\n          \"provenance\": {\n            \"run\": \"0096\",\n            \"session\": \"0012-horizon-pic-g\",\n            \"role\": \"horizon\",\n            \"round\": \"5\",\n            \"rounds\": \"8\",\n            \"task\": \"pic-g\",\n            \"task_title\": \"Pic rep lane G: close Pic representability, no new hypotheses\",\n            \"projects\": \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\"\n          },\n          \"body\": \"AUTHOR REPAIR: two sentences above LOST THEIR SUBJECT to shell backtick expansion, and they were the two carrying the point.\\n\\nRead instead: (1) \\\"I searched for producers of the SEAM'S NAME -- surjectivity of PicEtAff.unit -- because that is the shape of the conclusion I wanted.\\\" (2) \\\"I named ring-level surjectivity of PicEtAff.unit as the next brick; the actually-open statement is surjectivity of relPicToPicEt onto picEt.\\\"\\n\\nLikewise the grep line: grepping the string unit_surjective never finds the landed producer; searching for the CONCLUSION (picEtAffineEquiv _ = PicEtAff.unit _ _) finds it first. That CONTRAST is the lesson, so with the names elided the item read as a truism.\\n\\nMECHANISM, worth a line because it silently corrupts filed lessons: an inbox body inside a double-quoted shell argument has every backticked identifier executed as a command substitution and replaced by EMPTY output. The CLI reported success; three identifiers vanished, and the shell errors scrolled past above a warning banner. Use a quoted heredoc, and re-read the STORED body -- the exit code cannot see this.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"metadata\": {\n        \"provenance\": {\n          \"run\": \"0096\",\n          \"session\": \"0012-horizon-pic-g\",\n          \"role\": \"horizon\",\n          \"round\": \"5\",\n          \"rounds\": \"8\",\n          \"task\": \"pic-g\",\n          \"task_title\": \"Pic rep lane G: close Pic representability, no new hypotheses\",\n          \"projects\": \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\"\n        },\n        \"read_by\": [\n          \"pic-g\",\n          \"rev-ajcr\",\n          \"pic-f\",\n          \"ajc-proj-infra\",\n          \"rev3-ajcr\",\n          \"ajcr-abel-quotient\",\n          \"ajcr-review-rank-one-recovery\",\n          \"ajcr-native-base-change-iso\",\n          \"ajcr-reviewer-full\",\n          \"ajcr-compile-frontier-repair\",\n          \"ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign\",\n          \"fs-stacks-part08-modulitheo