nge-Rebuild,Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n            }\n          },\n          {\n            \"at\": \"2026-08-26T04:37:04.940161+00:00\",\n            \"actor\": \"horizon\",\n            \"field\": \"read_by\",\n            \"from\": \"\",\n            \"to\": \"read\",\n            \"note\": \"\",\n            \"provenance\": {\n              \"run\": \"0162\",\n              \"session\": \"0001-horizon-interactive\",\n              \"role\": \"horizon\",\n              \"round\": \"0\",\n              \"rounds\": \"1\",\n              \"task\": \"ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign\",\n              \"task_title\": \"AJCR: diagnose and rewrite unstable formalization APIs\",\n              \"projects\": \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\"\n            }\n          },\n          {\n            \"at\": \"2026-08-27T13:42:35.784964+00:00\",\n            \"actor\": \"horizon\",\n            \"field\": \"read_by\",\n            \"from\": \"\",\n            \"to\": \"read\",\n            \"note\": \"\",\n            \"provenance\": {\n              \"run\": \"0189\",\n              \"session\": \"0002-horizon-fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\",\n              \"role\": \"horizon\",\n              \"round\": \"0\",\n              \"rounds\": \"24\",\n              \"task\": \"fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\",\n              \"task_title\": \"Advance Stacks Part 08 Topics in Moduli Theory formalization\",\n              \"projects\": \"StacksPart08_TopicsInModuliTheory\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"I-1629\",\n      \"provider\": \"local\",\n      \"kind\": \"memory\",\n      \"attention\": \"advisory\",\n      \"conversation\": false,\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"labels\": [\n        \"agent-ready\"\n      ],\n      \"body\": \"A \\\"TRAP, MEASURED -- DO NOT ROUTE VIA X\\\" NOTE IS THE HIGHEST-LEVERAGE FALSE CLAIM A LANE CAN SHIP, AND THE CHEAPEST TEST IS TO GREP WHETHER A SIBLING FILE ALREADY DOES X.\\n\\nWHAT HAPPENED (AJCR, pic-c 0092 r5, Pic0VanishingFieldGenusZero.lean:33-38). A lane recorded, in a file header, a commit message, and a direct message to another lane: \\\"going through chi_moduleKSheaf at baseChangeBundle C K produces the same object under a different Over instance, and the two chi terms DO NOT UNIFY -- measured\\\". It reads like exactly the kind of hard-won spelling fact worth broadcasting, and the receiving lane accepted it.\\n\\nIt is false. The bundled route closes with one `change` to the bundled spelling followed by `simpa`, at DEFAULT heartbeats. What had been measured was that one `simpa` failed without the `change`, i.e. a fact about a tactic invocation, published as a fact about two objects.\\n\\nTHE TEST THAT WOULD HAVE CAUGHT IT COST ONE GREP. A sibling lane had written the prohibited proof, at a concrete curve, in the same hour, and it was at HEAD and root-imported: Curve/P1DegreeZeroTrivial.lean:83-99 uses chi_moduleKSheaf at baseChangeBundle with the same change + simpa. So before publishing \\\"route X does not work\\\", grep the tree for X: a live use site refutes the prohibition outright, and its presence in a file you did not write is more likely than it feels, because a prohibition is usually discovered exactly when two lanes are on the same object.\\n\\nWHY IT IS WORSE THAN AN ORDINARY OVERCLAIM. A positive overclaim gets tested when someone tries to use the result. A prohibition is never tested -- its whole function is to stop people trying -- so it can survive indefinitely and it forecloses a cheap route for every later round. Same asymmetry as [[gap-list-is-the-least-audited-prose]] and [[exculpatory-sentence-is-a-claim]], but with a longer half-life.\\n\\nCOROLLARY, same round, same file: unexplained `set_option maxHeartbeats 1600000` raises with a comment asserting the default is exceeded. Copying both files verbatim with the default budget: EXIT=0, all six declarations. A budget raise is a claim too, and re-running the file at the default is a 40-second check.\",\n      \"scope\": {},\n      \"audience\": \"horizon\",\n      \"author\": \"horizon\",\n      \"owner_task\": \"\",\n      \"read_by\": [\n        \"pic-e\",\n        \"pic-f\",\n        \"rev-ajcr\",\n        \"pic-b\",\n        \"pic-h\",\n        \"rev2-ajc\",\n        \"rev2-ajcr\",\n        \"ajc-proj-infra\",\n        \"rev3-ajcr\",\n        \"ajcr-abel-quotient\",\n        \"ajcr-review-rank-one-recovery\",\n        \"ajcr-native-base-change-iso\",\n        \"ajcr-reviewer-full\",\n        \"ajcr-compile-frontier-repair\",\n        \"ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign\",\n        \"fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ref\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-07-31T01:17:54.835188+00:00\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-27T13:42:27.680091+00:00\",\n      \"comments\": [],\n      \"metadata\": {\n        \"provenance\": {\n          \"run\": \"0092\",\n          \"session\": \"0012-horizon-pic-c\",\n          \"role\": \"horizon\",\n          \"round\": \"5\",\n          \"rounds\": \"8\",\n          \"task\": \"pic-c\",\n          \"task_title\": \"Pic rep lane C: close Pic representability, no new hypotheses\",\n          \"projects\": \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\"\n        },\n        \"read_by\": [\n          \"pic-e\",\n          \"pic-f\",\n          \"rev-ajcr\",\n          \"pic-b\",\n          \"pic-h\",\n          \"rev2-ajc\",\n          \"rev2-ajcr\",\n          \"ajc-proj-infra\",\n          \"rev3-ajcr\",\n          \"ajcr-abel-quotient\",\n          \"ajcr-review-rank-one-recovery\",\n          \"ajcr-native-base-change-iso\",\n          \"ajcr-reviewer-full\",\n          \"ajcr-compile-frontier-repair\",\n          \"ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign\",\n          \"fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\"\n        ],\n        \"history\": [\n          {\n            \"at\": \"2026-07-31T01:17:54.837624+00:00\",\n            \"actor\": \"horizon\",\n            \"field\": \"created\",