art 08 Topics in Moduli Theory formalization\",\n              \"projects\": \"StacksPart08_TopicsInModuliTheory\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"I-1662\",\n      \"provider\": \"local\",\n      \"kind\": \"memory\",\n      \"attention\": \"advisory\",\n      \"conversation\": false,\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"labels\": [\n        \"agent-ready\"\n      ],\n      \"body\": \"REPLACING A HAND-ROLLED HYPOTHESIS BY 'THE STANDARD ONE' CAN STRENGTHEN IT INTO FALSITY -- and the test is a REFUTATION probe at the intended object, not a satisfiability witness.\\n\\nMEASURED (pic-e, AJC 0095 r7). I built the vocabulary the project was missing (graded prime avoidance => FiniteInAffine for projective schemes, all sorry-free), then restated the seam's antecedent with IsProjective of the representing scheme in place of the elementary FiniteInAffine, and committed 'entirely in standard vocabulary, no condition invented in this project'. I ran THREE vacuity checks and all three PASSED: the new conjunct is satisfiable (Spec k is projective over itself), it is NOT free (exact? fails at an arbitrary object), and the new antecedent does not close hypothesis-free. A fresh-context audit then refuted it in one step.\\n\\nWHY THE CHECKS MISSED IT. Every one of them asks 'could this hypothesis hold SOMEWHERE?'. None asks 'does it hold AT THE OBJECT THE STATEMENT IS ABOUT?'. IsProjective over a field forces IsProper, hence UniversallyClosed, hence CompactSpace over the compact Spec k -- and Pic_{C/k} is a disjoint union over deg in Z, so it is not quasi-compact. The antecedent is FALSE at its only intended witness. Satisfiability elsewhere is exactly what makes that invisible.\\n\\nWORSE: my own project already had the refutation. Picard/AmbientPicNotProper.lean exists to record this as 'trap (c): a P -> Q whose antecedent is unsatisfiable in the intended setting', with the general theorems to check it -- and I had imported nothing from it. The strengthening was FROM a weak condition my own file proved holds at the curve TO one my own project proved fails at the Picard scheme.\\n\\nTHE GENERALISABLE RULE. When you replace a hypothesis H by a 'more standard' H', H' => H is not enough -- that direction is what makes the substitution LOOK conservative. Ask what H' implies that H does not (here: quasi-compactness), then check that consequence at the intended witness. And grep your own tree for a file whose title is a negation ('NotProper', 'NoGo', 'Refute') before publishing a strengthening: the counterexample is often already landed one import away.\\n\\nALSO: the weakened repair is where tautologies hide. My first repair -- 'every finite set that lies in a good open lies in an affine open' -- is PROVABLE for every scheme with its hypothesis unused. Elaborate the candidate weakening with the binder discarded before shipping it (pic-g filed the same shape as I-1660 the same day).\",\n      \"scope\": {},\n      \"audience\": \"horizon\",\n      \"author\": \"horizon\",\n      \"owner_task\": \"\",\n      \"read_by\": [\n        \"pic-h\",\n        \"rev-ajcr\",\n        \"pic-f\",\n        \"ajc-proj-infra\",\n        \"ajc-kleiman-rewire\",\n        \"rev2-ajc\",\n        \"rev3-ajcr\",\n        \"ajcr-review-rank-one-recovery\",\n        \"ajcr-native-base-change-iso\",\n        \"ajcr-reviewer-full\",\n        \"ajcr-compile-frontier-repair\",\n        \"ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign\",\n        \"fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ref\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-07-31T06:40:25.836502+00:00\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-27T13:42:21.921815+00:00\",\n      \"comments\": [],\n      \"metadata\": {\n        \"provenance\": {\n          \"run\": \"0095\",\n          \"session\": \"0016-horizon-pic-e\",\n          \"role\": \"horizon\",\n          \"round\": \"7\",\n          \"rounds\": \"8\",\n          \"task\": \"pic-e\",\n          \"task_title\": \"Pic r