tion APIs\",\n              \"projects\": \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\"\n            }\n          },\n          {\n            \"at\": \"2026-08-27T13:42:21.933296+00:00\",\n            \"actor\": \"horizon\",\n            \"field\": \"read_by\",\n            \"from\": \"\",\n            \"to\": \"read\",\n            \"note\": \"\",\n            \"provenance\": {\n              \"run\": \"0189\",\n              \"session\": \"0002-horizon-fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\",\n              \"role\": \"horizon\",\n              \"round\": \"0\",\n              \"rounds\": \"24\",\n              \"task\": \"fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\",\n              \"task_title\": \"Advance Stacks Part 08 Topics in Moduli Theory formalization\",\n              \"projects\": \"StacksPart08_TopicsInModuliTheory\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"I-0220\",\n      \"provider\": \"local\",\n      \"kind\": \"issue\",\n      \"attention\": \"advisory\",\n      \"conversation\": false,\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"labels\": [\n        \"agent-ready\"\n      ],\n      \"body\": \"HOUSE-RULE VIOLATION: Cohomology/RelCurveCollapse.lean is 752 lines (limit 500; rebuild charter constraint (3), worksheet Discipline, spec-dd-r Discipline clause).\\n\\nLanded at 2c16d3329 by the window-transport lane, which was killed by credit exhaustion immediately after committing and could not do the split it would normally have done (its sibling files respect the rule: WindowFieldTransport.lean 400 L).\\n\\nNOT urgent, NOT a correctness problem \\u2014 the file is green and kernel-covered (via 5b95cba0c's 8696-job root build) and its keystones are axiom-clean. But it must be split before Phase 2 (the Mathlib-extraction/alignment phase explicitly re-checks structure).\\n\\nSUGGESTED SPLIT (clean seams, from the module's own structure): (a) the datum + its 4-case gluing law (thetaChartDatum + laws) -> RelCurveCollapse.lean; (b) the sheaf collapse (thetaChartDatumSheafIso, componentwise glued/twist equiv) -> RelCurveCollapseSheaf.lean; (c) the class law (cechPicClass_thetaChartDatum, thetaFiberPullback, the fiberDivisor_ratioUnit_* computation) + the H1 seam -> RelCurveCollapseClass.lean. Statement-preserving; no proof changes; root gains two import lines.\\n\\nOWNER: any janitor/hygiene pass or the next lane that edits the file. Do NOT split while sibling lanes are consuming it mid-flight without checking horizon ps / live-lane state first.\",\n      \"scope\": {},\n      \"audience\": \"horizon\",\n      \"author\": \"human\",\n      \"owner_task\": \"\",\n      \"read_by\": [\n        \"pic-e\",\n        \"pic-f\",\n        \"rev-ajcr\",\n        \"pic-d\",\n        \"rev2-ajcr\",\n        \"ajc-proj-infra\",\n        \"ajcr-review-rank-one-recovery\",\n        \"ajcr-review-sepclosed-cover\",\n        \"ajcr-native-base-change-iso\",\n        \"ajcr-reviewer-full\",\n        \"ajcr-alignment-tags\",\n        \"ajcr-strategy-review\",\n        \"ajcr-compile-frontier-repair\",\n        \"ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign\",\n        \"fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ref\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-07-17T14:24:36.525300+00:00\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-27T13:42:19.031309+00:00\",\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"C-0001\",\n          \"item\": \"I-0220\",\n          \"author\": \"horizon\",\n          \"at\": \"2026-07-25T13:09:51.115592+00:00\",\n          \"provenance\": {\n            \"run\": \"0047\",\n            \"session\": \"0014-horizon-ajcr-w4-rep-free\",\n            \"role\": \"horizon\",\n            \"round\": \"6\",\n            \"rounds\": \"8\",\n            \"task\": \"ajcr-w4-rep-free\",\n            \"task_title\": \"Representability of Pic^0\",\n            \"projects\": \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\"\n          },\n          \"body\": \"**Still open, and the debt has grown (janitor audit, 2026-07-25).** Re-measured the rebuild's Lean tree against the 500-line charter constraint:\\n\\n- `Cohomology/RelCurveCollapse.lean` \\u2014 **752** lines (unchanged since this item was filed).\\n- `Picard/DivSchemeHighWindowFibreNormalization.lean` \\u2014 **721**\\n- `Picard/EntryIdeal.lean` \\u2014 **634**\\n- `Cohomology/GluedSheafModule.lean` \\u2014 **602**\\n- `Picard/DivSchemeAdaptationFibreRegular.lean` \\u2014 **597**\\n- `Cohomology/DatumDescent.lean` \\u2014 **558**, `Picard/DivSchemeHighWindowFibreModelBase.lean` \\u2014 **544**, `Cohomology/GluedSheafTermBaseChange.lean` \\u2014 **529**, `Picard/DivSchemeHighWindowTransitionSaturation.lean` \\u2014 **515**, plus three files at 501-503.\\n\\nSo this is a **twelve-file pattern**, not one violation. Worth noting that the split discipline has an independent payoff recorded elsewhere in the inbox: `I-0227` requires one heavy elaboration per compilation unit to stay under the machine's RSS ceiling, so oversized Picard files are also the OOM risk surface. Splitting them is the same work as respecting the charter.\\n\\nNo file was split by this pass \\u2014 that is proof-bearing source, outside a janitor's remit and outside the live certificate lane. Recording the measurement so the next owner sizes the job correctly.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"C-0002\",\n          \"item\": \"I-0220\",\n          \"author\": \"horizon\",\n          \"at\": \"2026-07-25T14:07:54.458914+00:00\",\n          \"provenance\": {\n            \"run\": \"0048\",\n            \"session\": \"0002-horizon-ajcr-w4-rep-free\",\n            \"role\": \"horizon\",\n            \"round\": \"0\",\n            \"rounds\": \"8\",\n            \"task\": \"ajcr-w4-rep-free\",\n            \"task_title\": \"Representability of Pic^0\",\n            \"projects\": \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\"\n          },\n          \"body\": \"**Count refreshed at HEAD (janitor hygiene pass, run 0048): the 500-line pattern is now fourteen files, not twe