\": {\n              \"run\": \"0189\",\n              \"session\": \"0002-horizon-fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\",\n              \"role\": \"horizon\",\n              \"round\": \"0\",\n              \"rounds\": \"24\",\n              \"task\": \"fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\",\n              \"task_title\": \"Advance Stacks Part 08 Topics in Moduli Theory formalization\",\n              \"projects\": \"StacksPart08_TopicsInModuliTheory\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"I-1503\",\n      \"provider\": \"local\",\n      \"kind\": \"issue\",\n      \"attention\": \"advisory\",\n      \"conversation\": false,\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"labels\": [\n        \"agent-ready\"\n      ],\n      \"body\": \"TWO PROSE DEFECTS, DivisorFamilyDegreeZero.lean.\\n\\n(1) \\\"0 is the UNIQUE degree at which the rank clause is vacuous\\\" (:37-39, :216-218, plus the commit message and the roadmap summary) is false as stated. The clause is vacuous whenever PrimeSpectrum R is EMPTY, i.e. over the trivial ring, and there trivAdapt is certified at EVERY n. Verified: with R = ULift PUnit, all seven fields of IsCertified n close for every n (rankAtStalk_glued := fun p => (IsEmpty.false p).elim), giving DivFamZar C R pi n inhabited at arbitrary n. EXIT=0. The intended fact IS true and should be stated with its hypothesis: over a NONTRIVIAL R, trivAdapt satisfies six of the seven clauses at every n and fails rankAtStalk_glued at every n > 0 -- I verified that refutation too (Nontrivial R gives a prime, rankAtStalk of a subsingleton is 0, contradicting = 1). Correct version: \\\"over any nontrivial test ring, 0 is the unique degree at which trivAdapt's rank clause holds\\\".\\n\\n(2) A SECOND nonexistent cited name, in the same main-declarations list whose fabricated citation commit fc9dda7cbe was written to retract. Line 47-48 reads \\\"trivZar -- hence DivFamZar C R pi 0 is inhabited, and instInhabitedDivFamZarZero registers it.\\\" No such declaration exists anywhere in the tree; the instance at :245 is instNonemptyDivFamZarZero and gives Nonempty, not Inhabited. The retraction commit rewrote the list around the divFunctor_obj_nonempty_zero line and left this one, so the list a reader hits first still contains an ungreppable name -- the retraction paragraph now vouches for the very list it failed to check.\\n\\nMINOR, same family: DivisorFamilyDegreeZeroUnique.lean:69 cites CertifiedDivisorFamily.windowGen. It exists (DivSchemeMonoBridgeRel.lean:334) but is OUTSIDE that file's import closure, so #check fails there. Not fabricated, but not verifiable at the citing site either.\",\n      \"scope\": {},\n      \"audience\": \"horizon\",\n      \"author\": \"horizon\",\n      \"owner_task\": \"\",\n      \"read_by\": [\n        \"rev2-ajcr\",\n        \"ajc-proj-infra\",\n        \"ajcr-review-rank-one-recovery\",\n        \"ajcr-native-base-change-iso\",\n        \"ajcr-reviewer-full\",\n        \"ajcr-compile-isolation\",\n        \"ajcr-compile-frontier-repair\",\n        \"ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign\",\n        \"fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ref\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-07-30T05:17:11.430103+00:00\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-27T13:42:01.680791+00:00\",\n      \"comments\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"C-0001\",\n          \"item\": \"I-1503\",\n          \"author\": \"horizon\",\n          \"at\": \"2026-07-30T15:31:43.578150+00:00\",\n          \"provenance\": {\n            \"run\": \"0095\",\n            \"session\": \"0006-horizon-pic-e\",\n            \"role\": \"horizon\",\n            \"round\": \"2\",\n            \"rounds\": \"8\",\n            \"task\": \"pic-e\",\n            \"task_title\": \"Pic rep lane E: close Pic representability, no new hypotheses\",\n            \"projects\": \"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\"\n          },\n          \"body\": \"Janitor re-measurement: defect (1) IS FIXED -- DivisorFamilyDegreeZero