}}, {"id": "I-2017", "provider": "local", "kind": "conversation", "body": "API search report\n\nNo existing theorem closes the first producer. Mathlib LocalRepresentability.representableBy/isRepresentable (AlgebraicGeometry/Sites/Representability.lean:192-208) is Zariski-local gluing only (sheaf + relatively representable open-immersion charts + local surjectivity). Fpqc.lean:109-123 gives EffectiveEpi for qc/flat/surjective schemes; EffectiveEpi.lean:82-100 gives desc/fac/uniq, but only descends morphisms equalizing kernel pairs, not schemes/objects/universal classes. CategoryTheory/Sites/Descent provides Pseudofunctor.DescentData, toDescentData, IsStack.isEquivalence_toDescentData and IsStackFor.essSurj, but no Scheme-valued stack instance exists in Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry. Project AlgebraDescent.lean comparison_bijective/descentEquiv/descentEquiv_naturality gives effective flat descent of commutative algebras only. Existing pic0RepresentableBy_finiteGaloisDescent (Pic0FiniteGaloisRepresentable.lean:35-54) requires OrbitsInAffineOpen; pic0RepresentableBy_of_baseChangeObjectIso (Pic0RepresentableByTransport.lean:75-81) only transports an existing representation along explicit object iso. Hence NO API eliminates finite-stage Pic0 RepresentableBy/universal-equivalence producer.\n\nPic0FiniteStageGluePackage.lean:39-91 and Pic0FiniteStageGeometry.lean:39-80 provide glued finite-type + quasi-compact only, no IsProjective/IsProper. Pic0FiniteStageOrbitAffine.lean:56-83,87-114,118-154 gives orbit affineness only under IsAlgClosed plus irreducible/connected represented-group assumptions, or explicit immersion/projectivity binder. No unconditional OrbitsInAffineOpen follows from the package; arbitrary-field orbit affineness remains separate.", "labels": ["agent-ready"], "status": "archived", "scope": {}, "audience": "task:ajcr-reviewer-full", "author": "horizon", "source_ref": null, "created_at": "2026-08-21T04:05:55.029128+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-08-21T05:04:42.797404+00:00", "metadata": {"conversation": true, "participants": ["task:ajcr-reviewer-full"], "started_by": "task:ajcr-reviewer-full", "read_by": ["ajcr-reviewer-full"], "provenance": {"run": "0149", "session": "0094-horizon-ajcr-reviewer-full", "role": "horizon", "round": "38", "rounds": "41", "task": "ajcr-reviewer-full", "task_title": "Fully answer the two AJCR reviewer PDFs \u2014 land pic0_representableBy and the Jacobian headline", "projects": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild,Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge"}, "comments": [{"id": "C-0001", "item": "I-2017", "author": "horizon", "at": "2026-08-21T04:08:09.835661+00:00", "provenance": {"run": "0149", "session": "0094-horizon-ajcr-reviewer-full", "role": "horizon", "round": "38", "rounds": "41", "task": "ajcr-reviewer-full", "task_title": "Fully answer the two AJCR reviewer PDFs \u2014 land pic0_representableBy and the Jacobian headline", "projects": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild,Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge"}, "body": "Exact signatures:\n\n- Fpqc instance: `{X Y : Scheme} (f : X \u27f6 Y) [QuasiCompact f] [Surjective f] [Flat f] : EffectiveEpi f`; fppf replaces QuasiCompact by LocallyOfFinitePresentation. EffectiveEpi.desc/fac/uniq are generic morphism descent.\n- LocalRepresentability.representableBy returns `F.1.RepresentableBy (glueData hf).glued`; isRepresentable returns `F.1.IsRepresentable`.\n- Pic0FiniteStageOrbitAffine orbit producers require IsAlgClosed plus irreducible/connected, or an explicit finite projective-space immersion (`i`, `hi`); the projective wrapper additionally requires `hproj : P.gluedMap.IsProjective`. Geometry only provides `locallyOfFiniteType_gluedMap` and `quasiCompact_gluedMap`."}, {"id": "C-0002", "item": "I-2017", "author": "horizon", "at": "2026-08-21T05:04:30.587780+00:00", "provenance": {"run": "0149", "session": "0096-horizon-ajcr-reviewer-full", "role": "horizon", "round": "39", "rounds": "41", "task": "ajcr-reviewer-full", "task_title": "Fully answer the two AJCR re