 "from": "", "to": "read", "note": "", "provenance": {"run": "0163", "session": "0008-horizon-ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign", "role": "horizon", "round": "2", "rounds": "7", "task": "ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign", "task_title": "AJCR: diagnose and rewrite unstable formalization APIs", "projects": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild"}}, {"at": "2026-08-27T08:33:46.419977+00:00", "actor": "horizon", "field": "read_by", "from": "", "to": "read", "note": "", "provenance": {"run": "0174", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-stacks-part08-modulitheory", "task_title": "Advance Stacks Part 08 Topics in Moduli Theory formalization", "projects": "StacksPart08_TopicsInModuliTheory"}}, {"at": "2026-08-27T08:47:39.429965+00:00", "actor": "horizon", "field": "read_by", "from": "", "to": "read", "note": "", "provenance": {"run": "0165", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-mumford", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-mumford", "task_title": "Advance Mumford Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Mumford"}}, {"at": "2026-08-27T09:59:27.705151+00:00", "actor": "horizon", "field": "read_by", "from": "", "to": "read", "note": "", "provenance": {"run": "0166", "session": "0004-horizon-fs-hartshorne", "role": "horizon", "round": "1", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-hartshorne", "task_title": "Advance Hartshorne Algebraic Geometry formalization", "projects": "Hartshorne"}}]}}, {"id": "I-2036", "provider": "local", "kind": "conversation", "body": "Milne reconnaissance: low-dependency candidates\n\nRead-only findings. Basic.lean is placeholder only. Best first node: lem:milne-5-8 / Base change for sections, blueprint/src/ch01-geometry.tex:1536-1552. Exact statement: for commutative R, a hom alpha:M->N between free rank-one R-modules, surjective implies bijective; consequently a surjective map of invertible sheaves is an isomorphism. Lean-friendly core signature: theorem surj_rankOne_bijective [CommRing R] {M N : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] [Module.Free R M] [Module.Free R N] [Module.Finite R M] [Module.Finite R N] (hM : Module.finrank R M = 1) (hN : Module.finrank R N = 1) (f : M ->\u2097[R] N) (hf : Function.Surjective f) : Function.Bijective f. Proof via bases, reducing to multiplication by r; surjectivity gives IsUnit r. No graph deps.\n\nBackup 1: lem:milne-index-determinant, ch01:1190-1207. Finite-rank free Z-lattice endomorphism alpha rationally invertible implies index (Lambda : alpha Lambda)=|det alpha|; moderate finite-index API effort.\n\nBackup 2: lem:milne-polynomial-function, ch01:1240-1258. Line-restrictions polynomial over infinite field imply multivariate polynomial function; no deps, but requires choosing a formal definition via MvPolynomial.\n\nBackup 3: lem:milne-5-10, ch01:1573-1587. Canonical multiplication map S tensor_R M -> M, s tensor m maps to sm; can use TensorProduct.lift, but is more a construction than theorem. Geometry defs (group variety/rational maps) have high setup with no local wrappers.", "labels": ["agent-ready"], "status": "archived", "scope": {}, "audience": "task:root", "author": "horizon", "source_ref": null, "created_at": "2026-08-27T08:41:30.668320+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-08-27T09:02:41.981427+00:00", "metadata": {"conversation": true, "participants": ["task:root", "task:fs-milne"], "started_by": "task:fs-milne", "read_by": ["fs-milne"], "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}, "comments": [{"id": "C-0001", "item": "I-2036", "author": "horizon", "at": "2026-08-27T08:43:14.668632+00:00", "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}, "body": "Correction on signature\n\nModule.finrank requires a division ring, so the suggested rank hypotheses are best stated over a field (faithful special case), or avoided by supplying explicit bases eM : Basis (Fin 1) R M and eN : Basis (Fin 1) R N. For exact arbitrary-commutative-ring statement, use those bases and coordinate map; surjectivity of the resulting 1x1 matrix gives its entry a right inverse, hence a unit in a commutative ring, yielding injectivity. The field specialization is likely the cleanest first Lean declaration."}, {"id": "C-0002", "item": "I-2036", "author": "horizon", "at": "2026-08-27T08:44:10.993418+00:00", "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}, "body": "Additional prioritization\n\nIf exact arbitrary-ring generality is mandatory, choose lem:milne-5-10 instead: blueprint ch01:1573-1587 only asks for canonical map S tensor_R M -> M, and mathlib TensorProduct.lift gives it directly with map_tmul proof. It is dependency-free and can be made a clean declaration in Basic.lean. Base-change rank-one remains the best substantive theorem, but should be scoped explicitly with supplied `Basis (Fin 1) ...` to preserve ring generality."}, {"id": "C-0003", "item": "I-2036", "author": "horizon", "at": "2026-08-27T09:02:38.971744+00:00", "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}, "body": "Reconnaissance consumed: the rank-one map unit is now committed in Milne; no further response is pending on this thread."}], "history": [{"at": "2026-08-27T08:41:30.673405+00:00", "actor": "horizon", "field": "created", "from": "", "to": "open", "note": "opened", "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0