 "conversation", "body": "API findings for Part01 preliminaries\n\nPart01 wrappers are in StacksPart01Lib/Topology.lean, Categories.lean, Spectrum.lean. Exact reusable declarations: StacksPart01.isQuasiCompactMap_comp {f:X\u2192Y}{g:Y\u2192Z} (hf) (hg); image_retrocompact hf; image_quasiCompact (hX : QuasiCompactSpace X) (hf : Continuous f); closed_subset_quasiCompact hs ht hsub; closed_subset_of_quasiCompact_space hX ht; quasiCompact_iff_closed [CompactSpace X] [T2Space X]; quasiCompact_isClosed [T2Space X]; quasiCompact_union hs ht; quasiCompact_prod hs ht; quasiCompact_inter [T2Space X] hs ht; hausdorff_iff_closed_diagonal X (exact t2_iff_isClosed_diagonal).\n\nSpectrum wrappers: StacksPart01.mem_standardOpen_iff (f:R) (x:PrimeSpectrum R): x\u2208basicOpen f \u2194 f\u2209x.asIdeal (exact PrimeSpectrum.mem_basicOpen); standardOpen_mul f g (exact PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen_mul); standardOpen_one/zero; isOpen_standardOpen f.\n\nCategory wrappers: StacksPart01Lib.isIso_iff_exists_inverse; inverse_unique; isGroupoid_iff_all_isIso; isIso_mono_of/isIso_epi_of. Underlying Mathlib exact facts include IsCompact.image, IsCompact.union/prod/inter, IsClosed.isCompact [CompactSpace], isCompact_univ, isCompact_range, isCompact_diagonal, isCompact_iff_compactSpace, Set.Finite.isCompact_biUnion, Finset.isCompact_biUnion; Set.image_preimage_eq_inter_range. CategoryTheory.IsIso.hom_inv_id/inv_hom_id, IsIso.inv_eq_of_hom_inv_id, IsIso.inv_ext, IsGroupoid.all_isIso.\n\nGraph frontier shows highest-value unimplemented Part01 labels include Zariski topology, Functoriality of spectrum, Localization exact, Matrix left inverse, Universal property localization module, Idempotent spec, Spec closed, Product ideals in prime. No sibling project has stronger Part01 wrappers; downstream projects use native IsCompact and AlgebraicGeometry.quasiCompact. Note MainProjects/.phase0-pre snapshot is stale/unrelated.", "labels": ["agent-ready"], "status": "open", "scope": {}, "audience": "task:ajcr-finite